Fict: The File Integrity Checking Tool

DESCRIPTION
Fict is a lightweight command line script that performs checks 
on the contents of a directory in order to determine if they were modified. 
Additionally, it generates alerts regarding file changes if detected.

GENERAL USE
While it can be used on any directory, Fict works best on limited-access data sets 
that are not routinely modified. To use Fict, follow these instructions:

In the directory you have downloaded Fict in, run the command: “python3 fict.py”. 
Fict will peform the file integrity check using the information you have provided
it in the fict.conf configuration file, including hash function and target directories.
The time taken by Fict to perform the integrity check may vary by directory size and contents. 
During the first integrity check performed, Fict will create a baseline file containing the initial 
files in your directories, each mapped to its own calculated checksum. 
This value is crucial in determining if the content in your directories has been modified, 
as a single change in the document including adding/deleting a character, will alter the 
entire checksum for the file. Additionally, Fict will analyze the directory in further 
integrity checks for new or deleted files. 

Access the file integrity results in the file named “results.json”, with the name
of the hash function used coming after 'results' and before '.json'. If the file 
does not exist on the first integrity check, Fict will create it edit it after each 
subsequent file integrity check. Here, you will find all 
relevant information pertaining to the analysis including any detected changes, if any exist.

